# Entes MPR-53CS.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | ENTES MPR-53CS 3-Phase Power Analyzer (Modbus RTU RS-485)
# | 
# | Source: entes-mpr-53cs-modbus-register-map-en.pdf (01.12.2019)
# | Protocol: Modbus RTU; FC03 read, FC06 write single register
# | All measurements use 32-bit format — each data point occupies 2 consecutive Modbus registers.
# | Addresses are word addresses; address N = Modbus register N (first of a 32-bit pair).
# | Addresses increment by 2 for each measurement entry.
# | 
# | Scale factors (from visible MULTIPLIER column):
# | Voltage:       raw × 0.01 = V  (includes VT ratio; max range ×VT ×Vmax)
# | Current:       raw × 0.001 = A (includes CT ratio)
# | Active/reactive power: raw × 0.01 = W/VAr (signed)
# | Apparent power: raw × 0.01 = VA
# | Power factor:  raw × 0.001 = dimensionless (-1.000..1.000, signed)
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Entes
@model=MPR-53CS
@vendor_website=entes.com.tr
@description=3-phase power analyzer, Modbus RTU. 32-bit registers (2 words each, addr+=2 per entry). Measurements at addr 0-52: L1-L2/L2-L3/L3-L1 line voltages, L1-N/L2-N/L3-N phase voltages (×0.01 V), L1/L2/L3/N currents (×0.001 A), total+per-phase active/reactive/apparent power (×0.01 W/VAr/VA), power factor L1/L2/L3/total (×0.001), frequency (×0.01 Hz). Min/max/demand and energy counters (import/export active, inductive/capacitive reactive × 2 tariffs) at higher addresses. Setpoints (up to 10) at 0x8000 (32768): activation, parameter type, high/low set, fail/recovery delay, hysteresis, output, parameter (8 registers each).
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/entes-mpr-53cs.toml; Source: entes-mpr-53cs-modbus-register-map-en.pdf (01.12.2019). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
@x_origin=omniconsole

